 "description": "When asked what this database spends its time on: captured pg_stat_statements query shapes ranked by exec time, calls, or mean. Needs no database connection; reads the local history (dryrun snapshot capture --streams query, or init's best-effort capture) and is empty when no capture carries query stats. Each entry is tagged with its reporting node and never averaged across nodes: a primary and a replica are different workloads. A node label that rotates between servers reports only the server that answered its newest capture; _meta.hint says so when the captures show it. SQL is qshape-normalized and parameterized, never the literal text or parameter values a user ran. Counters are cumulative since the last reset, not a recent-activity rate. It reports the newest capture per node and differences nothing, so it says what the corpus has cost since that reset, never what it cost this week; snapshot_diff kind=query is what differences them, and _meta.history, when present, says what the local store holds. An empty result carrying unknown: true means no capture holds query stats at all, which is not the same as a database whose statements are all cheap. Before comparing or differencing any two numbers, read _meta.hint -- it carries the caveats that decide whether they are comparable at all.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "properties": {
   "limit": {
    "default": 50,
    "description": "Max results (default 50, 0 for all).",
    "type": "number"
   },
   "min_calls": {
    "default": 2,
    "description": "Skip entries with fewer calls than this (default 2) to filter one-shot noise.",
    "type": "number"
   },
   "node": {
    "description": "Filter to one node label. Omit to see all nodes' queries together (each entry still tagged with its own node).",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "offset": {
    "default": 0,
    "description": "Skip N results.",
    "type": "number"
   },
   "sort": {
    "default": "total_time",
    "description": "Sort by: 'total_time' (default, total_exec_time_ms), 'calls', or 'mean_time' (mean_exec_time_ms).",
    "enum": [
     "total_time",
     "calls",
     "mean_time"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "required": [],
  "type": "object"
 },
